1. What do props help us accomplish?
    - Add variable data into functions, allowing more reusability


2. How do you pass a prop into a component?
    - Add it into a React function as if it was a HTML attribute;
    <FunctionName 
        prop1:"one"
        prop2:"two"
    />


3. Can I pass a custom prop (e.g. `blahblahblah={true}`) to a native
   DOM element? (e.g. <div blahblahblah={true}>) Why or why not?
   - No, since native elements have their own pre-determined properties.
     Custom functions allow custom props, since you create the custom ones from the ground.


4. How do I receive props in a component?
   - Add the name of the propas a parameter and the name of the data in curly brackets 
function Navbar(props) {
    return (
        <header>
            <h1>{prop.name}</h1>
        </header>
    )
}


5. What data type is `props` when the component receives it?
    Object